Who is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. 
 The Zhang lab seeks to hire a postdoctoral fellow whose duties will include: 
 Conducting independent research in bioinformatics, comparative genomics, structural analysis, and machine learning; 
 Preparing manuscripts and grant proposals and contributing to securing external research funding; 
 Mentoring graduate and undergraduate students and contributing to a collaborative research environment; 
 Presenting research findings at national and international scientific conferences and publishing in leading peer-reviewed journals. 
